{{- /*
  rclone — mise-managed, mount-capable (macOS, work + personal profiles).

  Homebrew's rclone formula hard-refuses `rclone mount` on macOS
  ("rclone mount is not supported on MacOS when rclone is installed via
  Homebrew") — live-proven, not a hypothetical. mise's default backend for
  rclone, aqua:rclone/rclone, instead ships the official upstream GitHub
  release binaries: cmount-tagged (`rclone version` shows `go/tags: cmount`)
  and mount-capable — verified live on this machine, including a mount
  attempt reaching `mount_macfuse` (the same "it got as far as the kext"
  proof the old custom-builds installer relied on).

  Unlike the CMake case (cmake.toml.tmpl) — where Gatekeeper quarantines
  Kitware's prebuilt CMake.app and refuses to run it — the rclone CLI
  binary aqua installs runs cleanly with no quarantine friction; it's a
  bare executable, not an app bundle. So no source-build workaround is
  needed here, just the aqua-backed prebuilt.

  clipboard-mount (home/dot_local/libexec/executable_clipboard-mount) is
  the sole consumer: its SFTP-over-MacFUSE peer mount is why rclone exists
  in this repo at all. It resolves the mise shim off PATH for interactive
  callers, with a hardcoded shim-path fallback for the headless launchd
  clipboard-bridge service, whose PATH has no shims dir.

  mise loads every conf.d/*.toml alongside config.toml, so this layers the
  tool in without templating the main config (same pattern as
  cmake.toml.tmpl / dev-shell.toml.tmpl).

  Scope: macOS, work + personal profiles (the same pair the zsh
  custom-build targets) — the work laptop is a sit-at machine in the
  clipboard pair and mounts its peers too. Mount support needs macFUSE;
  the Brewfile cask is personal-gated but the work laptop carries macFUSE
  already (restic scrub), and a machine without it just degrades to the
  lazy rsync/Ctrl-Y flow (clipboard-mount fails soft).
*/ -}}
{{- if and (eq .chezmoi.os "darwin") (or (eq .profile "work") (eq .profile "personal")) }}
[tools]
rclone = "latest"
{{- else }}
# Not installed: this profile has no clipboard-mount consumer for it
# (see the header comment above for the full rationale).
{{- end }}
